## F-STATE-001 - persisted ordinal instead of a durable key

- **Discovered:** <YYYY-MM-DD>, <PR_OR_ITEM>
- **Symptom:** After a release that inserts, removes or reorders items in an
  ordered collection (a curriculum, a menu, a pipeline, a migration list),
  saved state points at the wrong thing. Nothing errors; the system simply
  resumes at a different place than it stopped.
- **Root cause:** The state file stored a position - index 7 - rather than the
  identity of the thing at that position. The ordinal is only meaningful
  relative to a list that has since changed.
- **Check:** Persisted references are durable identifiers: names, slugs,
  stable ids. Where an ordinal must be kept for compatibility, version the
  state format and write a loader that resolves name first, falls back to the
  old ordinal, and clamps. Test the migration with a mutation: reorder the
  collection in the test and assert the restored state still points at the same
  item.
- **Command:** `<STATE_ROUNDTRIP_TEST_COMMAND>`
- **Note:** the reference deployment hit this when a learning frontier persisted as a bare index
  into a ladder that later gained a rung.

